<div class="col lede" style="margin-top: 28px">
  <p>I built the same small API gateway twice, once in Ruby on master and once in Go, and pushed both with wrk on the same four cores. The first version of this page was too kind to Ruby: almost all of its time went into C, sockets and the kernel. This version makes Ruby do the work. It parses HTTP into objects, rewrites headers, runs a chain of middleware and reshapes JSON in Ruby, and it shares a rate limiter, a response cache and its metrics between Ractors with no IPC, no Redis and no files.</p>
  <p>Go is still <%= times(raw4[:go], raw4[:ruby]) %> faster at plain proxying. On the JSON route Ruby beats Go's standard library and loses to a hand-written Go filter. What changed is that one Ruby process now does what used to take a pool of forks plus Redis: every Ractor sees the same counters, the same cache and the same limits, and they run in parallel.</p>
</div>

<div class="wide board" style="margin-top: 30px" aria-label="Headline results">
  <%- duel = ->(rows) { top = rows.map(&:last).max; rows.map { |label, cls, value| [label, cls, value, (value * 78.0 / top).round(1)] } } -%>
  <%- [
        ["Plain proxying, 4 cores", duel.([["Go", "c-go", raw4[:go]], ["Ruby", "c-ruby", raw4[:ruby]]]), "<b>Go is #{times(raw4[:go], raw4[:ruby])} faster.</b> Requests per second through header rewriting and keep-alive on both legs."],
        ["API rewrite, 4 cores", duel.([["Ruby", "c-ruby", api4[:ruby]], ["Go jsontext", "c-go-soft", api4[:jt]], ["Go stdlib", "c-go", api4[:go]]]), "<b>#{api4[:ruby] > api4[:go] ? "Ruby is #{times(api4[:ruby], api4[:go])} faster than encoding/json" : "Go's encoding/json is #{times(api4[:go], api4[:ruby])} faster"}.</b> #{lead("A hand-written Go filter", api4[:jt], "Ruby", api4[:ruby]).sub(" is ", " runs ")}."],
        ["Rate limit of 1,000/s, over 10 s", duel.([["Ractors", "c-ruby", limit["ruby-ractor"]], ["4 forks", "c-ruby-soft", limit["ruby-fork"]], ["Go", "c-go", limit["go-std"]]]), "<b>Forks let through #{times(limit["ruby-fork"], limit["ruby-ractor"])} the limit.</b> Each process counts on its own; Ractors share one counter."],
        ["Cache of 1,000 URLs, over 10 s", duel.([["Ractors", "c-ruby", fetches["ruby-ractor"]], ["4 forks", "c-ruby-soft", fetches["ruby-fork"]], ["Go", "c-go", fetches["go-std"]]]), "<b>Forks hit the backend #{times(fetches["ruby-fork"], fetches["ruby-ractor"])} as often.</b> Upstream fetches with a 1-second TTL; Ractors share one cache."],
      ].each do |title, rows, verdict| -%>
